# Contract ownership for ai-business-contracts.
#
# ACCEPTANCE_CRITERIA.md M0-CON-015 requires every catalog contract to have
# exactly one authoritative owner. This file is the review-time counterpart:
# it makes the owner's approval mechanically required before a contract change
# can merge. A contract without an owner is invalid.
#
# Cross-repository note: entries here name reviewers for CHANGES MADE IN THIS
# REPOSITORY. They do not transfer contract authority. Database, auth, agent
# runtime, channel, admin web, and infrastructure contracts remain owned by
# their repositories - see governance/OWNERSHIP.md.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                       @siansoft-sian

# Contract source. Changes here are consumer-visible and require owner review
# plus a passing compatibility check (governance/CHANGE_PROCESS.md).
/contracts/             @siansoft-sian
/catalog/               @siansoft-sian
/compatibility/         @siansoft-sian
/templates/             @siansoft-sian

# Governance and boundary enforcement. Weakening a gate requires explicit
# review; HARNESS.md section 7 forbids obtaining green CI by loosening one.
/governance/            @siansoft-sian
/scripts/               @siansoft-sian
/tests/                 @siansoft-sian
/.github/               @siansoft-sian
